# Keyword exceptions for the image build. Keep empty if possible — stable amd64 only.
media-libs/libva-intel-media-driver ~amd64  # no stable amd64 ebuild in tree at this snapshot
x11-drivers/nvidia-drivers           ~amd64  # no stable amd64 ebuild in tree at this snapshot

# The ONLY ~amd64 package in the desktop set, and a deliberate departure from the rule in the
# line above — recorded here rather than slipped in. Plasma Login Manager shipped with Plasma
# 6.6 as KDE's SDDM replacement and has no stable ebuild yet; x11-misc/sddm does
# (0.21.0_p20250502-r1), so this exception is the price of choosing PLM (plan/09). It is worth
# paying because PLM reuses kwin as its greeter compositor rather than starting a second one,
# which matters in an image that is Wayland-only by construction.
#
# Pinned to =6.6.6 deliberately, not left open: both 6.6.6-r1 and 6.7.4-r1 raise QTMIN to
# >=6.11.2, which is itself ~amd64 and would pull a ~amd64 Qt AND the ~amd64 Plasma 6.7.4 set
# in behind it. 6.6.6 needs only QTMIN=6.10.0, satisfied by the stable dev-qt/qtbase-6.11.1.
# One ~amd64 package, not a hundred.
# Drop the pin — not the entry — when 6.7.x stabilises alongside the rest of Plasma.
=kde-plasma/plasma-login-manager-6.6.6   ~amd64

# Everything else in @desktop is stable amd64 at the pinned snapshot, verified against the
# tree rather than assumed: Plasma 6.6.6, Frameworks 6.27.0, Gear 26.04.3, dev-qt/qtbase-6.11.1.
# Baloo's tail needs no entry either — kde-frameworks/{baloo,kfilemetadata} at 6.27.0,
# kde-apps/baloo-widgets at 26.04.3, and dev-db/lmdb, media-libs/taglib, media-gfx/exiv2 are
# all stable amd64.
#
# If "emerge -p @desktop" reports any OTHER masked-by-keyword package, that is new information:
# add it here with the same one-line justification, and reconsider whether the set has drifted.

# ---- the installer (plan/16) ---------------------------------------------------------------
# NOT a preference, and not a departure from the "stable amd64 only" rule so much as the only
# way this package resolves at all. Measured against the pinned tree on 2026-08-28: the stable
# revision is REFUSED outright, before any version choice is made —
#
#   !!! The ebuild selected to satisfy "app-admin/calamares" has unmet requirements.
#   - app-admin/calamares-3.3.14-r4 … PYTHON_SINGLE_TARGET="-python3_12 -python3_13"
#     The following REQUIRED_USE flag constraints are unsatisfied:
#       exactly-one-of ( python_single_target_python3_12 python_single_target_python3_13 )
#
# because this image is on python 3.14 (=dev-lang/python-3.14.6_p1, admitted deliberately — see
# plan/06's "Python — RESOLVED again at the first Plasma build") and BOTH stable calamares
# revisions cap at PYTHON_COMPAT=python3_{11..13}. Only 3.3.14-r8 and 3.4.2-r1 carry
# python3_{12..14}, and both are ~amd64. The alternative — adding python3_13 as a second
# PYTHON_TARGET so the stable ebuild resolves — would put a SECOND interpreter in every image
# this config root builds, including the product one, to avoid one keyword line. That is
# strictly worse.
#
# Deliberately unpinned, unlike the plasma-login-manager entry above, because the two entries are
# not the same shape. That one is pinned because a newer revision drags a ~amd64 Qt and the whole
# ~amd64 Plasma set in behind it — the pin contains a blast radius. Here there is nothing to
# contain: calamares is a leaf, no package in the tree depends on it, and it is emerged by ONE
# profile that is never released. Which revision this resolves to is recorded, like everything
# else, in config/portage/lock/installer.lock.
#
# It reaches only the live medium. config/portage/expected-packages.desktop.txt names none of
# it, and stage 50 fails the build on unexplained additions, so this line cannot leak into the
# product by being forgotten.
app-admin/calamares                  ~amd64
